{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi6qnnGQ9sneh2u75LnF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ticket 08 is finished and everything is committed. `npm test` passes (195), as do `npm run test:hydration` (86 + 17), `npm run test:hydration-dev` (17) and `npm run typecheck:hydration`. `npm run lint` still reports 2 errors, both unused variables in `test/plugins.ts`. That file came from an earlier merged branch and is outside this ticket, so I didn't fix them.\n\n[x] Every route's response, including the 404, contains exactly one state script with the fixed id, placed before the module script\n[x] The script's content parses as JSON and round-trips: `State(parsed)` serializes back to an equal object\n[x] `route` in the payload is the request path without the prefix; an unknown path keeps the requested path\n[x] `?count=12` on the index route yields `count` 12 in the payload\n[x] A non-integer, non-finite, or non-numeric `count` falls back to 5\n[x] A request path containing `</script>` cannot close the state script: the document still has one state script that parses\n[x] `assemble` throws when the state marker is missing or duplicated, and when the page marker is missing or duplicated\n[x] `State()` with no input and `State` with a partial input both fill defaults for missing keys\n[x] Each static mutator changes only its own signal\n[x] ADR-008 exists with a row in the index\n[x] `npm run test:hydration`, `npm run test:hydration-dev`, and `npm run typecheck:hydration` pass\n\nWhat changed:\n1. **`example-hydration/state.ts`:** `AppState` has four signals: `route`, `count`, `noticeOpen` and `labels`. `State(partial?)` fills in defaults (`/`, 5, false, and the three labels). The mutators are `State.increase`, `decrease`, `openNotice`, `dismissNotice`, `addLabel` and `removeLabel`. `serialize` sits beside them, and the types come from `microtags`.\n2. **`server/scaffold.ts`:** adds `STATE_MARKER`, `STATE_ID` (`microtags-state`) and `stateScript()`, which writes a JSON script with `<` escaped. `assemble(scaffold, body, state)` throws unless each marker appears exactly once.\n3. **`index.html`:** the state marker now sits just before the module script.\n4. **`server/app.ts`:** every handler, including `notFound`, builds state for its request. The `count` query parameter is accepted only if it is a plain whole number (a safe integer); anything else gets the default of 5.\n\nThe tests were in `test/hydration.ts` and failed first, then passed. `test/hydration-dev.ts` and `test/hydration-listen.ts` needed no changes.\n\nI added ADR-008 and its row in the index, plus a note in `AGENTS.md` about the state marker and `assemble`.\n\nThis worktree had no `node_modules` or `dist/`, so I ran `npm install` and `npm run build` before testing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":165,"cache_read_input_tokens":67931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":165},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5fbb6ff4-e9e2-4d4b-82ba-b3e509eceb14","uuid":"eb6bbd92-0077-44a5-9d34-1e02f0f42382","timestamp":"2026-10-04T23:56:30.795Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi6qn4MYpwCKHt5HVj7g"}
